:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CALL.Call Program (CALL)
:P.Use the Call Program (CALL) command to call a program with
parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALL/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALL/PARM'.Parameters (PARM)
:P.The parameters passed to the program, in order.
:P.Up to 255 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.hexadecimal-value:EPV.
:PD.Type the value as characters or as hexadecimal digits in X'...'.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CALLPRC.Call Procedure (CALLPRC)
:P.Use the Call Procedure (CALLPRC) command to call a bound procedure
with parameters passed by reference or by value.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALLPRC/PRC'.Procedure (PRC)
:P.The procedure for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALLPRC/PARM'.Parameters (PARM)
:P.The parameters passed to the program, in order.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Value
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.hexadecimal-value:EPV.
:PD.Type the value as characters or as hexadecimal digits in X'...'.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Passing method
:P.Also accepted&colon. *BYREF, *BYVAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALLPRC/RTNVAL'.CL var for return value (RTNVAL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CALLSUBR.Call Subroutine (CALLSUBR)
:P.Use the Call Subroutine (CALLSUBR) command to call a subroutine of
the procedure.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALLSUBR/SUBR'.Subroutine (SUBR)
:P.The subroutine for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CALLSUBR/RTNVAL'.CL var for return value (RTNVAL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGVAR.Change Variable (CHGVAR)
:P.Use the Change Variable (CHGVAR) command to assign the value of an
expression to a CL variable.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGVAR/VAR'.CL variable name (VAR)
:P.The CL variable name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGVAR/VALUE'.New value (VALUE)
:P.The new value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLOSE.Close File (CLOSE)
:P.Use the Close File (CLOSE) command to close a declared file so that
the next RCVF reopens it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLOSE/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DCL.Declare CL Variable (DCL)
:P.Use the Declare CL Variable (DCL) command to declare a CL variable.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/VAR'.CL variable name (VAR)
:P.The CL variable name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/TYPE'.Type (TYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*DEC:EPK.
:PD.Decimal.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LGL, *INT, *UINT, *PTR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/STG'.Storage (STG)
:P.The storage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DEFINED, *BASED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/LEN'.Length (LEN)
:P.The length for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Length
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be at least 1.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Decimal positions
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 9.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/VALUE'.Initial value (VALUE)
:P.The initial value for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.hexadecimal-value:EPV.
:PD.Type the value as characters or as hexadecimal digits in X'...'.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/DEFVAR'.Defined on variable (DEFVAR)
:P.The defined on variable for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Variable
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Position
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCL/BASPTR'.Basing pointer (BASPTR)
:P.The basing pointer for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DCLF.Declare File (DCLF)
:P.Use the Declare File (DCLF) command to declare a file whose record
formats give the procedure its field variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/ALWVARLEN'.Allow variable length fields (ALWVARLEN)
:P.Whether to allow variable length fields.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/ALWNULL'.Allow null value fields (ALWNULL)
:P.Whether to allow null value fields.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLF/ALWGRAPHIC'.Allow graphic fields (ALWGRAPHIC)
:P.Whether to allow graphic fields.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DCLPRCOPT.Declare Processing Options (DCLPRCOPT)
:P.Use the Declare Processing Options (DCLPRCOPT) command to set the
compile and bind options of a CL procedure from inside its source.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/SUBRSTACK'.Subroutine stack depth (SUBRSTACK)
:P.The subroutine stack depth for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 20 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 99 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/LOG'.Log commands (LOG)
:P.The log commands for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/ALWRTVSRC'.Allow RTVCLSRC (ALWRTVSRC)
:P.Whether RTVCLSRC can retrieve the source from the program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/TEXT'.Description (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/DFTACTGRP'.Default activation group (DFTACTGRP)
:P.Whether to default activation group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/ACTGRP'.Activation group (ACTGRP)
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*CALLER:EPK.
:PD.The activation group of the caller.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STGMDL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/STGMDL'.Storage model (STGMDL)
:P.The storage model of the program's automatic and static
storage&colon. single-level, teraspace, or inherited from the activation
group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNGLVL:EPK.
:PD.Single-level storage.
:PT.:PK.*TERASPACE:EPK.
:PD.Teraspace storage.
:PT.:PK.*INHERIT:EPK.
:PD.Inherited from the activation group.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/BNDDIR'.Binding directory (BNDDIR)
:P.The binding directories the binder searches for modules and service
programs to resolve imports.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DCLPRCOPT/BNDSRVPGM'.Bind service program (BNDSRVPGM)
:P.The service programs bound by reference to the program.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Service program
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Activation
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.At once, without waiting.
:PT.:PK.*DEFER:EPK.
:PD.Later, when it is needed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DMPCLPGM.Dump CL Program (DMPCLPGM)
:P.Use the Dump CL Program (DMPCLPGM) command to print the variables and
messages of the running CL procedure.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DO.Do (DO)
:P.Use the Do (DO) command to open a group of commands that ENDDO
closes.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DOFOR.Do For (DOFOR)
:P.Use the Do For (DOFOR) command to open a group that repeats while an
integer variable counts from one value to another.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOFOR/VAR'.CL variable name (VAR)
:P.The CL variable name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOFOR/FROM'.From value (FROM)
:P.The from value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOFOR/TO'.To value (TO)
:P.The to value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOFOR/BY'.Increment (BY)
:P.The increment for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DOUNTIL.Do Until (DOUNTIL)
:P.Use the Do Until (DOUNTIL) command to open a group that repeats until
a condition holds, tested at the end of each pass.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOUNTIL/COND'.Condition (COND)
:P.The condition for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DOWHILE.Do While (DOWHILE)
:P.Use the Do While (DOWHILE) command to open a group that repeats while
a condition holds.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DOWHILE/COND'.Condition (COND)
:P.The condition for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ELSE.Else (ELSE)
:P.Use the Else (ELSE) command to run a command when the preceding IF
condition did not hold.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ELSE/CMD'.Command to run (CMD)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDDO.End Do (ENDDO)
:P.Use the End Do (ENDDO) command to close a DO, DOWHILE, DOUNTIL or
DOFOR group.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDPGM.End Program (ENDPGM)
:P.Use the End Program (ENDPGM) command to close a CL procedure.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDRCV.End Receive (ENDRCV)
:P.Use the End Receive (ENDRCV) command to cancel a RCVF or SNDRCVF that
was issued with WAIT(*NO).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDRCV/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDRCV/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDRCV/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDSELECT.End Select (ENDSELECT)
:P.Use the End Select (ENDSELECT) command to close a SELECT group.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ENDSUBR.End Subroutine (ENDSUBR)
:P.Use the End Subroutine (ENDSUBR) command to close a subroutine and
return a value to CALLSUBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDSUBR/RTNVAL'.Return value (RTNVAL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=GOTO.Go To (GOTO)
:P.Use the Go To (GOTO) command to continue at a labelled command.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='GOTO/CMDLBL'.Command label (CMDLBL)
:P.The command label for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=IF.If (IF)
:P.Use the If (IF) command to run a command when a condition holds.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='IF/COND'.Condition (COND)
:P.The condition for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='IF/THEN'.Command to run (THEN)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ITERATE.Iterate (ITERATE)
:P.Use the Iterate (ITERATE) command to skip to the next pass of a
DOWHILE, DOUNTIL or DOFOR group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ITERATE/CMDLBL'.Command label (CMDLBL)
:P.The command label for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LEAVE.Leave (LEAVE)
:P.Use the Leave (LEAVE) command to leave a DOWHILE, DOUNTIL or DOFOR
group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LEAVE/CMDLBL'.Command label (CMDLBL)
:P.The command label for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=MONMSG.Monitor Message (MONMSG)
:P.Use the Monitor Message (MONMSG) command to monitor for escape,
notify and status messages and run a command when one arrives.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MONMSG/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MONMSG/CMPDTA'.Comparison data (CMPDTA)
:P.The comparison data for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 28 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MONMSG/EXEC'.Command to run (EXEC)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=OTHERWISE.Otherwise (OTHERWISE)
:P.OTHERWISE starts the group of commands of a SELECT group that runs
when no WHEN condition is true. It is valid only in a CL program or
procedure.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='OTHERWISE/CMD'.Command to run (CMD)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PGM.Program (PGM)
:P.Use the Program (PGM) command to open a CL procedure and name its
parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PGM/PARM'.Parameters (PARM)
:P.The parameters passed to the program, in order.
:P.Up to 255 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RCVF.Receive File (RCVF)
:P.Use the Receive File (RCVF) command to read a record from the
declared file into its field variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVF/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVF/WAIT'.Wait for record (WAIT)
:P.Whether to wait for record.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RCVF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RETURN.Return (RETURN)
:P.Use the Return (RETURN) command to return to the caller of the
current program.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTNSUBR.Return from Subroutine (RTNSUBR)
:P.Use the Return from Subroutine (RTNSUBR) command to return from a
subroutine before its ENDSUBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTNSUBR/RTNVAL'.Return value (RTNVAL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 0 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVCFGSTS.Retrieve Configuration Status (RTVCFGSTS)
:P.Use the Retrieve Configuration Status (RTVCFGSTS) command to put the
status of a configuration description into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCFGSTS/CFGD'.Configuration description (CFGD)
:P.The configuration description for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCFGSTS/CFGTYPE'.Type (CFGTYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIN, *CTL, *NWI, *NWS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCFGSTS/STSCDE'.CL var for STSCDE (5 0) (STSCDE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of STSCDE. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVCFGSTS/STS'.CL var for STS (20) (STS)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of STS. Give a character
variable of at least 20 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 20 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVJOBA.Retrieve Job Attributes (RTVJOBA)
:P.Use the Retrieve Job Attributes (RTVJOBA) command to put the
attributes of the current job into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOB'.CL var for JOB (10) (JOB)
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/USER'.CL var for USER (10) (USER)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of USER. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/NBR'.CL var for NBR (6) (NBR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of NBR. Give a character
variable of at least 6 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/LOGLVL'.CL var for LOGLVL (1 0) (LOGLVL)
:P.How much of the job's messages are written to the job log, from 0
(none) to 4 (all).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/LOGSEV'.CL var for LOGSEV (2 0) (LOGSEV)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of LOGSEV. Give a decimal
variable of 2 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/LOGCLPGM'.CL var for LOGCLPGM (4) (LOGCLPGM)
:P.Whether the commands that CL programs run are written to the job log.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/OUTQ'.CL var for OUTQ (10) (OUTQ)
:P.The output queue the spooled files go to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/OUTQLIB'.CL var for OUTQLIB (10) (OUTQLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of OUTQLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/PRTDEV'.CL var for PRTDEV (10) (PRTDEV)
:P.The printer device the spooled output prints on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/INQMSGRPY'.CL var for INQMSGRPY (10) (INQMSGRPY)
:P.How inquiry messages sent to the job are answered&colon. by the
operator, with their default replies, or from the system reply list.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/BRKMSG'.CL var for BRKMSG (7) (BRKMSG)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of BRKMSG. Give a character
variable of at least 7 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/STSMSG'.CL var for STSMSG (7) (STSMSG)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of STSMSG. Give a character
variable of at least 7 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DEVRCYACN'.CL var for DEVRCYACN (13) (DEVRCYACN)
:P.What happens to the job when its display device has an error&colon. a
message is sent, the request is ended, or the job is ended.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/TSEPOOL'.CL var for TSEPOOL (10) (TSEPOOL)
:P.Whether the job moves to the base pool when its time slice ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/PRTTXT'.CL var for PRTTXT (30) (PRTTXT)
:P.Up to 30 characters printed at the bottom of every page of the job's
printed output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/PRTKEYFMT'.CL var for PRTKEYFMT (10) (PRTKEYFMT)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of PRTKEYFMT. Give a
character variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SRTSEQ'.CL var for SRTSEQ (10) (SRTSEQ)
:P.The sort sequence table that orders and compares character
data&colon. the hexadecimal values, the job's, a language's (shared or
unique weights), or a table by name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SRTSEQLIB'.CL var for SRTSEQLIB (10) (SRTSEQLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SRTSEQLIB. Give a
character variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/LANGID'.CL var for LANGID (3) (LANGID)
:P.The language identifier&colon. three letters naming the language
whose sort sequence is used.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/CNTRYID'.CL var for CNTRYID (2) (CNTRYID)
:P.The country or region identifier&colon. two letters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/CCSID'.CL var for CCSID (5 0) (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DFTCCSID'.CL var for DFTCCSID (5 0) (DFTCCSID)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of DFTCCSID. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/CHRIDCTL'.CL var for CHRIDCTL (10) (CHRIDCTL)
:P.How the character identifier of display and printer files is
handled&colon. the device's or the job's CCSID.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SWS'.CL var for SWS (8) (SWS)
:P.The eight job switches&colon. 0 for off, 1 for on, X for unchanged.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/ACGCDE'.CL var for ACGCDE (15) (ACGCDE)
:P.The accounting code the job's resources are charged to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DATE'.CL var for DATE (6) (DATE)
:P.The job date.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/CURLIB'.CL var for CURLIB (10) (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SYSLIBL'.CL var for SYSLIBL (165) (SYSLIBL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SYSLIBL. Give a character
variable of at least 165 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 165 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/USRLIBL'.CL var for USRLIBL (2750) (USRLIBL)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of USRLIBL. Give a character
variable of at least 2750 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 2750 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/TYPE'.CL var for TYPE (1) (TYPE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of TYPE. Give a character
variable of at least 1 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/RUNPTY'.CL var for RUNPTY (2 0) (RUNPTY)
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/TIMESLICE'.CL var for TIMESLICE (7 0) (TIMESLICE)
:P.How long, in milliseconds, a thread of the job runs before another
thread of the same priority gets the processor.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/PURGE'.CL var for PURGE (4) (PURGE)
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DFTWAIT'.CL var for DFTWAIT (7 0) (DFTWAIT)
:P.How many seconds the system waits for an instruction to complete
before it signals a time-out.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 7 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DDMCNV'.CL var for DDMCNV (5) (DDMCNV)
:P.Whether conversations to remote systems for DDM are kept or dropped
when nothing is using them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DATFMT'.CL var for DATFMT (4) (DATFMT)
:P.The format of dates&colon. the order of year, month and day.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DATSEP'.CL var for DATSEP (1) (DATSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a date.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/TIMSEP'.CL var for TIMSEP (1) (TIMSEP)
:P.The character between the parts of a time.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/DECFMT'.CL var for DECFMT (1) (DECFMT)
:P.The decimal format&colon. the character used for the decimal point
and how zeros print before it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/ENDSTS'.CL var for ENDSTS (1) (ENDSTS)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of ENDSTS. Give a character
variable of at least 1 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SBMMSGQ'.CL var for SBMMSGQ (10) (SBMMSGQ)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SBMMSGQ. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SBMMSGQLIB'.CL var for SBMMSGQLIB (10) (SBMMSGQLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SBMMSGQLIB. Give a
character variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SBSD'.CL var for SBSD (10) (SBSD)
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SBSDLIB'.CL var for SBSDLIB (10) (SBSDLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SBSDLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBD'.CL var for JOBD (10) (JOBD)
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBDLIB'.CL var for JOBDLIB (10) (JOBDLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of JOBDLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBQ'.CL var for JOBQ (10) (JOBQ)
:P.The job queue, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBQLIB'.CL var for JOBQLIB (10) (JOBQLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of JOBQLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBPTY'.CL var for JOBPTY (1 0) (JOBPTY)
:P.The priority of the job on the job queue, from 1 (highest) to 9
(lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/OUTPTY'.CL var for OUTPTY (1 0) (OUTPTY)
:P.The priority of the job's spooled files on the output queue, from 1
(highest) to 9 (lowest).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 1 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/SPLFACN'.CL var for SPLFACN (10) (SPLFACN)
:P.What happens to the job's spooled files when the job ends&colon. they
are kept with the job or detached from it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/LOGOUTPUT'.CL var for LOGOUTPUT (10) (LOGOUTPUT)
:P.When the job log is produced as a spooled file&colon. by the job
itself at its end, by a server job afterwards, or not at all.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBMSGQMX'.CL var for JOBMSGQMX (2 0) (JOBMSGQMX)
:P.The largest size of the job's message queue, in megabytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/JOBMSGQFL'.CL var for JOBMSGQFL (10) (JOBMSGQFL)
:P.What happens when the job's message queue fills&colon. the job ends,
the queue wraps, or messages are printed and then overwritten.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/CURUSER'.CL var for CURUSER (10) (CURUSER)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of CURUSER. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVJOBA/TIMEZONE'.CL var for TIMEZONE (10) (TIMEZONE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of TIMEZONE. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVMBRD.Retrieve Member Description (RTVMBRD)
:P.Use the Retrieve Member Description (RTVMBRD) command to put the
description of a database file member into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/MBR'.Member (MBR)
:P.The member for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FIRSTMBR, *LASTMBR.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Relationship
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NEXT:EPK.
:PD.The next one.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/RTNLIB'.CL var for RTNLIB (10) (RTNLIB)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of RTNLIB. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/RTNSYSTEM'.CL var for RTNSYSTEM (4) (RTNSYSTEM)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of RTNSYSTEM. Give a
character variable of at least 4 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/RTNMBR'.CL var for RTNMBR (10) (RTNMBR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of RTNMBR. Give a character
variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/FILEATR'.CL var for FILEATR (5) (FILEATR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of FILEATR. Give a character
variable of at least 5 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/FILETYPE'.CL var for FILETYPE (5) (FILETYPE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of FILETYPE. Give a character
variable of at least 5 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/SRCTYPE'.CL var for SRCTYPE (10) (SRCTYPE)
:P.The type of the source member&colon. CLLE, RPGLE, PF, CMD and so on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/CRTDATE'.CL var for CRTDATE (13) (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/EXPDATE'.CL var for EXPDATE (7) (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/TEXT'.CL var for TEXT (50) (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/NBRCURRCD'.CL var for NBRCURRCD (10 0) (NBRCURRCD)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of NBRCURRCD. Give a decimal
variable of 10 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/NBRDLTRCD'.CL var for NBRDLTRCD (10 0) (NBRDLTRCD)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of NBRDLTRCD. Give a decimal
variable of 10 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/DTASPCSIZ'.CL var for DTASPCSIZ (15 0) (DTASPCSIZ)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of DTASPCSIZ. Give a decimal
variable of 15 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/ACCPTHSIZ'.CL var for ACCPTHSIZ (15 0) (ACCPTHSIZ)
:P.The largest size the file's access paths can reach.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 15 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/NBRDTAMBRS'.CL var for NBRDTAMBRS (5 0) (NBRDTAMBRS)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of NBRDTAMBRS. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/CHGDATE'.CL var for CHGDATE (13) (CHGDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of CHGDATE. Give a character
variable of at least 13 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/SAVDATE'.CL var for SAVDATE (13) (SAVDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SAVDATE. Give a character
variable of at least 13 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/RSTDATE'.CL var for RSTDATE (13) (RSTDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of RSTDATE. Give a character
variable of at least 13 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/NBRDAYUSED'.CL var for NBRDAYUSED (5 0) (NBRDAYUSED)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of NBRDAYUSED. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/USEDATE'.CL var for USEDATE (7) (USEDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of USEDATE. Give a character
variable of at least 7 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/SRCCHGDATE'.CL var for SRCCHGDATE (13) (SRCCHGDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SRCCHGDATE. Give a
character variable of at least 13 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 13 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMBRD/JOINMBR'.CL var for JOINMBR (4) (JOINMBR)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of JOINMBR. Give a character
variable of at least 4 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVMSG.Retrieve Message (RTVMSG)
:P.Use the Retrieve Message (RTVMSG) command to put a message
description from a message file, with its substitution data filled in,
into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/MSGID'.Message identifier (MSGID)
:P.A message identifier&colon. three letters and four hexadecimal
digits, CPF1234 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/MSGF'.Message file (MSGF)
:P.The message file that holds the message descriptions, by name and
library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/MSGDTA'.Message data field values (MSGDTA)
:P.The values substituted for the message's variables.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 512 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/MSG'.CL var for MSG (132) (MSG)
:P.The text of the message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 132 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/MSGLEN'.CL var for MSGLEN (5 0) (MSGLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of MSGLEN. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/SECLVL'.CL var for SECLVL (3000) (SECLVL)
:P.The second-level text of the message&colon. what it means and what to
do.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 3000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/SECLVLLEN'.CL var for SECLVLLEN (5 0) (SECLVLLEN)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of SECLVLLEN. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/SEV'.CL var for SEV (2 0) (SEV)
:P.A message severity from 0 to 99. Higher numbers mean more serious
conditions.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 2 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/ALROPT'.CL var for ALROPT (9) (ALROPT)
:P.Whether an alert is sent when the message is sent, and when.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 9 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/LOGPRB'.CL var for LOGPRB (4) (LOGPRB)
:P.Whether a problem is logged for the message.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/CCSID'.CCSID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*JOB:EPK.
:PD.The value of the job.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVMSG/TXTCCSID'.CL var for TXTCCSID (5 0) (TXTCCSID)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of TXTCCSID. Give a decimal
variable of 5 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 5 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVOBJD.Retrieve Object Description (RTVOBJD)
:P.Use the Retrieve Object Description (RTVOBJD) command to put the
description of an object into CL variables.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVOBJD/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVOBJD/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
