:P.The CL variable that receives the value of PWDCHGBLK. Give a
character variable of at least 10 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVUSRPRF/USREXPDATE'.CL var for USREXPDATE (7) (USREXPDATE)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of USREXPDATE. Give a
character variable of at least 7 characters.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVUSRPRF/USREXPITV'.CL var for USREXPITV (3 0) (USREXPITV)
:P.The CL variable that receives the value of USREXPITV. Give a decimal
variable of 3 digits, 0 after the point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SELECT.Select (SELECT)
:P.Use the Select (SELECT) command to open a group of WHEN and OTHERWISE
choices.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDF.Send File (SNDF)
:P.Use the Send File (SNDF) command to write a record format of the
declared display file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDF/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDRCVF.Send/Receive File (SNDRCVF)
:P.Use the Send/Receive File (SNDRCVF) command to write a record format
of the declared display file and read the reply.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRCVF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRCVF/RCDFMT'.Record format (RCDFMT)
:P.The record format.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRCVF/WAIT'.Wait for record (WAIT)
:P.Whether to wait for record.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDRCVF/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SUBR.Subroutine (SUBR)
:P.Use the Subroutine (SUBR) command to open a subroutine of the
procedure.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SUBR/SUBR'.Subroutine (SUBR)
:P.The subroutine for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=TFRCTL.Transfer Control (TFRCTL)
:P.Use the Transfer Control (TFRCTL) command to end the current program
and call another in its place.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRCTL/PGM'.Program (PGM)
:P.The program the command calls or works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='TFRCTL/PARM'.Parameters (PARM)
:P.The parameters passed to the program, in order.
:P.Up to 255 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.variable-name:EPV.
:PD.Type the name of a CL variable, starting with &amp..
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WAIT.Wait (WAIT)
:P.Use the Wait (WAIT) command to complete a RCVF or SNDRCVF that was
issued with WAIT(*NO).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WAIT/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.The value of the file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WAIT/OPNID'.Open file identifier (OPNID)
:P.The open file identifier the file was opened with.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WHEN.When (WHEN)
:P.Use the When (WHEN) command to one choice of a SELECT group, taken
when its condition holds.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WHEN/COND'.Condition (COND)
:P.The condition for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WHEN/THEN'.Command to run (THEN)
:P.The command to run for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.command:EPV.
:PD.Type a command.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
